gradients: [("The prompt may be too focused on assessing the truthfulness of statements based on job titles, party affiliations, and general reliability of similar claims, rather than the specific content and verifiability of the statement itself. This approach might lead to incorrect predictions when the statement's truthfulness is not strongly correlated with the provided context or when the statement is objectively false but lacks relevant cues in the context to signal this. Additionally, the prompt's emphasis on potential biases may not adequately account for situations where the statement's truthfulness can be evaluated independently of these factors, leading to misclassification of clear falsehoods.", '## Example 1\nText: "Statement: The high-speed rail project would create 60,000-plus jobs for Floridians.\nJob title: U.S. Representative\nState: Florida\nParty: democrat\nContext: an interview with WESH-TV"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 2\nText: "Statement: The wealth gap between blacks and whites in the United States is greater than the black-white wealth gap was in apartheid South Africa.\nJob title: \nState: \nParty: none\nContext: a broadcast of "The Daily Show""\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 3\nText: "Statement: On a cap-and-trade plan.\nJob title: \nState: \nParty: republican\nContext: a letter to the Minnesota delegation in Washington"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 4\nText: "Statement: A proposed immigration bill will bankrupt Georgia if passed.\nJob title: \nState: \nParty: libertarian\nContext: a press release"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No')]
